  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Support to ESNFI Cluster Partners Responding to the 22 June Earthquake in Paktika and Khost</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 21 June 2022 Afghanistan earthquake primarily impacted the provinces of Paktika, Paktia, and Khost, resulting in extensive damage to buildings in the affected areas and over 13,000 families affected. In addition to loss of life and devastating injury, the earthquake has resulted in the destruction of critical infrastructure - including homes, health facilities, schools, and water networks - leaving thousands vulnerable to further harm. In coordination with the Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Item (ESNFI) Cluster and the Office of the Humanitarian Coordinator, IOM will engage Miyamoto to carry out two activities: conduct a geotechnical survey of the affected area, to address concerns regarding ongoing seismic risk; and provide ongoing technical support to the ESNFI Cluster and partner actors to improve the capacity of the cluster to undertake rapid vernacular repairs.</narrative>
  </description>
